    "created_at": "2021-09-09T11:07:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-09T11:07:31Z",
    "body": "Should probably  be noted that Resize Observer actually extends the rendering step to [include styles recalc and layout update](https://drafts.csswg.org/resize-observer/#html-event-loop) but they don't go as far as defining these steps, which we might want?\r\nAlso, I don't think there is a \"wrong\" or \"correct\" behavior here, (but of course it is possible that the exposed behavior isn't the one intended by the implementers) I believe that historically UAs were free to do the reflow when they wanted as an optimization, as long as it's been done before the rendering. For instance IIRC webkit may do that update at idle, and not necessarily wait the rendering frame, and authors themselves can force re-layout by calling [some methods](https://gist.github.com/paulirish/5d52fb081b3570c81e3a) so if we do define these algorithms these points should probably be taken into consideration.\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
