    "created_at": "2021-09-16T09:32:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-16T09:32:47Z",
    "body": "I am saying that this is currently not specified, so there is no \"correct\" or \"wrong\" behavior here.\r\nWe might want to define one, but currently there isn't.  \r\nI *guess* that if browsers have such various behaviors based on the event type it's a mix of implementation bugs (FF behavior with \"click\" doesn't seem deterministic at all) and optimizations quirks (IIRC some UI events are throttled to the painting frame, which will probably have some influence here), but you as a web author should not expect a fixed behavior.   \r\nIf you want a deterministic behavior, you need to either force a reflow manually, or to wait after the next repaint. Everything in between is currently under-specified and up to each implementation.",
